1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,630
Can satellites actually see tornadoes?

2
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:09,242
Usually, the funnels are too small to pick
out in these weather-satellite images.

3
00:00:09,541 --> 00:00:15,043
But NASA and NOAA recorded something much
bigger in April twenty-eleven: vast storm

4
00:00:15,043 --> 00:00:17,760
systems moving across the American South.

5
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:23,347
Afterward, other satellites revealed thin
brown corridors where trees and vegetation

6
00:00:23,347 --> 00:00:24,669
had been ripped away.

7
00:00:24,969 --> 00:00:26,963
The storm clouds moved on.

8
00:00:27,263 --> 00:00:28,647
The scars stayed.
